WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.060
- [John] At the top of the
track right before a race,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.110
I tell myself there's nothing I can't do.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.670
People have died doing
this, and I know that.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:14.130
But going 90 miles per
hour is so damn fun.

00:00:16.979 --> 00:00:19.396
(soft music)

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.330
My name is John Daly,

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.500
and I'm a two time
Olympic skeleton slider.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.060
The skeleton track is
roughly one mile long

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.090
and I'll slide up to 90 miles per hour

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.770
with my face only one inch off the ice.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.930
You get a green light, and
you take off sprinting

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.571
and you can't hear a thing.

00:00:41.571 --> 00:00:44.720
(heartbeat pounding)

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.150
When I make contact with the sled,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.450
it feels like a place
I've been my whole life.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.160
Last 15 years I've made that
same jump onto the sled.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:01.380
You could feel immense pressure
as you're pulling five g's,

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.980
so my eight pound head
now weighs 40 pounds.

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:13.200
If you start to get stiff,
you start to get scared,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.380
it's not gonna work; the
sled's gonna break loose on you

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.430
and you are gonna crash.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.020
You have to embrace the speed

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.630
instead of getting afraid of it.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.070
At the bottom of the skeleton race,

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.630
when I've had a really good run,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.510
I feel like I could run through the wall.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.760
You're so pumped up, and
that's why I love it.

